          },
          "evidence_mark_platform_8146ff": {
            "summary": "- The canonical project root is `F:\\Mark-XLVIII-main`.\n- The current repository snapshot is `1f86e8cba90bebd0507eb0ae1cfe0db670e9b66ad768d175c1178e7b46749ec4`.\n- JARVIS read 36 selected files and skipped 4 sensitive files.",
            "updated_at": "2026-09-24T21:08:05Z"
          }
        }
      },
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "source_identification",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "role: research\nproject: resource_library\n\nThe Resource Library findings below are already real evidence from a completed, read-only scan (project_operator learn_project has already run -- you do not need to run anything yourself, and nothing in the evidence is asking you to authorize or invoke a tool). Using ONLY that evidence and the self-assessment's subject-area list above, write the actual mapping report now: for each subject area, name which catalogued resources are genuinely relevant and explain why. Produce the report itself, not a plan or process for producing one later. If the self-assessment above is itself a caveat that its own evidence was too thin to enumerate real subject areas, say so explicitly and note that this mapping cannot proceed meaningfully until a fuller scan is available -- do not invent subject areas to map against.\n\nDeliverables:\n- Report linking subject areas to relevant Resource Library entries, or an explicit note that the upstream self-assessment was too thin to map against\n\n<!-- jarvis-forward-scout: do not edit below this line -->\n> **Context from `evidence_resource_library_3ac86a`:** - The canonical project root is `D:\\Resource-Library`.\n- The current repository snapshot is `ec88bab6703d18570e4c45cefd66124cc18812aaf6b7a6fc0c9774a9c0c07e30`.\n- JARVIS read 36 selected files and skipped 0 sensitive files.\n> **Context from `self_assessment_ad3289`:** Caveat: The provided evidence contains only scan metadata (a root path, a repository snapshot hash, and file read/skip counts) with no descriptive content about what the code does. Therefore, subject areas cannot be enumerated.\n\nNo subject-area list is provided because the evidence does not support any claim about the platform's actual subsystems.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 640,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 180,
      "deliverables": [
        "Report linking subject areas to relevant Resource Library entries"
      ],
      "jarvis": {
        "layout_profile": "dependency",
        "layout_baseline": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 640,
          "width": 420,
          "height": 180
        },
        "kind": "plan_step",
