    {
      "id": "synthesize_objectives",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "role: research\n\nCombine the self‑assessment list and the source‑identification report to craft 3‑5 concrete, individually actionable research objectives. Each objective must be specific enough to guide real research steps and must not merely restate existing functionality.\n\nDeliverables:\n- List of 3‑5 concrete research objectives",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 960,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 180,
      "deliverables": [
        "List of 3‑5 concrete research objectives"
      ],
      "jarvis": {
        "layout_profile": "dependency",
        "layout_baseline": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 960,
          "width": 420,
          "height": 180
        },
        "kind": "plan_step",
        "step_id": "synthesize_objectives_88106c",
        "workflow_id": "mark_rd_scouting",
        "run_id": "mark_rd_scouting-v7",
        "step_state": "ACCEPTED",
        "attempt": 1,
        "updated_at": "2026-09-24T21:08:05Z"
      },
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "review_synthesis",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "role: review\n\nCheck that the objectives produced by the synthesis step are genuinely concrete, individually actionable, non-redundant with Mark-XLVIII's existing functionality, and grounded in the real self-assessment and source-identification evidence rather than generic aspirations.\n\nDeliverables:\n- Pass/fail assessment of the synthesized objectives, with reasons",
      "x": 500,
      "y": 960,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 180,
      "deliverables": [
        "Pass/fail assessment of the synthesized objectives, with reasons"
      ],
      "jarvis": {
        "layout_profile": "dependency",
        "layout_baseline": {
          "x": 500,
          "y": 960,
          "width": 420,
          "height": 180
        },
        "kind": "plan_step",
        "step_id": "review_synthesis_5556f0",
        "workflow_id": "mark_rd_scouting",
        "run_id": "mark_rd_scouting-v7",
        "step_state": "ESCALATE",
        "attempt": 1,
        "updated_at": "2026-09-24T21:08:05Z"
      },
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "phase_plan",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "role: research\n\nFor each research objective, break it into ordered steps, assign dependency ordering, and group objectives that can be pursued independently into separate branches (e.g., Branch A, Branch B) to allow parallel work. Produce the full phased plan ready for review.\n\nDeliverables:\n- Complete phased research plan with branch structure and step ordering",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1280,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 180,
      "deliverables": [
        "Complete phased research plan with branch structure and step ordering"
      ],
      "jarvis": {
        "layout_profile": "dependency",
        "layout_baseline": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 1280,
          "width": 420,
          "height": 180
        },
        "kind": "plan_step",
        "step_id": "phase_plan_5610f6",
        "workflow_id": "mark_rd_scouting",
        "run_id": "mark_rd_scouting-v7",
        "step_state": "PENDING",
        "attempt": 0,
        "updated_at": "2026-09-24T21:08:05Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "review_final_plan",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "role: review\n\nIndependently check the full phased research plan for internal consistency: dependency ordering is correct, branches genuinely can run in parallel, and no phase silently depends on unstated prior work.\n\nDeliverables:\n- Pass/fail assessment of the phased plan's internal consistency, with reasons",
      "x": 500,
      "y": 1280,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 180,
      "deliverables": [
        "Pass/fail assessment of the phased plan's internal consistency, with reasons"
      ],
